                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink-900">
              2. The Centered Mobile Safe Area: Stop Channel Art Cropping
            </h3>
            <p>
              YouTube displays your channel banner across diverse hardware, ranging from 75-inch smart TVs down to 6-inch mobile screens. Rather than reformatting the file, YouTube centers the 2560 × 1440 image and crops it dynamically. The critical area visible on mobile phones is constrained to a centered <strong>{mobileCropWidth} × {mobileCropHeight} px</strong> viewport.
            </p>
            <p>
              All aesthetic backgrounds in our library are mathematically arranged so that main focal motifs, anime characters, and decorative borders either frame the safe area naturally or span across widescreen margins. To test custom artwork before uploading, inspect it with our interactive <a href="/tools/youtube-banner-checker" class="text-accent underline font-medium hover:text-accent-600">YouTube banner checker</a> or read the <a href="/guides/youtube-banner-safe-area" class="text-accent underline font-medium hover:text-accent-600">banner safe area guide</a>.
